1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:01,820
(All characters and organisations in this drama are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,820 --> 00:00:02,850
(Filming with minors followed broadcast guidelines,)

3
00:00:02,850 --> 00:00:03,850
(and generative AI was used in select scenes.)

4
00:00:05,560 --> 00:00:07,520
(Episode 7)

5
00:00:09,990 --> 00:00:12,160
- Mister. - Yes?

6
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:15,300
You know my mom well, right?

7
00:00:18,170 --> 00:00:20,770
A long time ago. I mean, eight years ago.

8
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:23,170
You've met my mom before, haven't you?

9
00:00:34,050 --> 00:00:35,250
I knew it.

10
00:00:37,390 --> 00:00:38,960
Did you and my mom like each other?

11
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:42,390
Do you still like her?

12
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:46,160
No.

13
00:00:46,560 --> 00:00:48,930
I'm not interested in married people.

14
00:00:57,740 --> 00:00:58,910
You're getting it all over your face.

15
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:07,720
You're not eating your potatoes?

16
00:01:09,650 --> 00:01:10,650
Eat them.

17
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:31,440
I thought the world was a huge place,

18
00:01:31,510 --> 00:01:34,040
but it's surprisingly small, isn't it?

19
00:01:40,820 --> 00:01:43,090
Back then, why did you...

20
00:01:44,490 --> 00:01:45,920
leave him?

21
00:01:47,890 --> 00:01:49,130
That's in the past.

22
00:01:50,160 --> 00:01:51,830
I'd rather not talk about it.

23
00:01:53,030 --> 00:01:54,030
I see.

24
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:57,270
I guess there's no reason you have to answer me.

25
00:01:58,200 --> 00:01:59,940
But I just happened to...

26
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:03,310
discover your lie, Gyu Rim.

27
00:02:04,370 --> 00:02:07,810
That you've never been married,

28
00:02:08,950 --> 00:02:12,250
and that you lied to Mu Jin.

29
00:02:12,950 --> 00:02:14,120
So...

30
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:16,550
maybe...

31
00:02:18,090 --> 00:02:20,920
that boy you call your son...

32
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:24,130
is Mu Jin's son.

33
00:02:24,130 --> 00:02:25,630
The possibility is now much higher.

34
00:02:26,860 --> 00:02:28,670
I really don't want to get involved.

35
00:02:28,730 --> 00:02:31,570
Then don't. Stay out of other people's business.

36
00:02:34,640 --> 00:02:37,540
Mu Jin isn't other people to me.

37
00:02:39,980 --> 00:02:41,280
My Gyeol...

38
00:02:42,410 --> 00:02:44,450
has nothing to do with Mu Jin.

39
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:46,550
You two broke up eight years ago,

40
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:48,290
and you say your son is eight years old.

41
00:02:48,620 --> 00:02:49,750
Even if you only know basic math,

42
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:51,690
how can he possibly have nothing to do with him?

43
00:02:54,590 --> 00:02:55,930
I'm sorry but...

44
00:02:56,530 --> 00:02:59,630
- I can't listen to accusations. - Gyu Rim...

45
00:03:00,330 --> 00:03:02,000
I don't know who gave you the right...

46
00:03:02,070 --> 00:03:03,900
to misunderstand things as you please,

47
00:03:03,970 --> 00:03:05,870
make assumptions, and get things wrong.

48
00:03:08,070 --> 00:03:10,340
Don't interfere in someone else's life...

49
00:03:10,410 --> 00:03:11,410
so recklessly.

50
00:03:12,310 --> 00:03:13,940
We ended things a long time ago,

51
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:16,980
and my Gyeol is my son.

52
00:03:17,310 --> 00:03:19,320
He has absolutely nothing to do with Mu Jin.

53
00:03:29,730 --> 00:03:31,030
Did you hear that, Kim Mu Jin?

54
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:33,660
She said no.

55
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:35,970
Even if I don't believe her,

56
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:37,970
you believe her, you punk.

57
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:43,810
Ma'am, I'll get it.

58
00:03:45,810 --> 00:03:48,380
Hey, who was that young man?

59
00:03:48,850 --> 00:03:51,080
You looked so shocked when you saw him.

60
00:03:52,880 --> 00:03:57,120
Well, if it's awkward to talk about, then forget it.

61
00:03:58,820 --> 00:04:00,660
It's not like that. It's just...

62
00:04:01,260 --> 00:04:04,330
He's someone I used to know, and I ran into him unexpectedly.

63
00:04:04,390 --> 00:04:05,900
Oh, please.

64
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:10,830
I thought perhaps he was your old flame.

65
00:04:10,830 --> 00:04:12,600
Right, right.

66
00:04:13,470 --> 00:04:16,270
To be honest, as a potential flame for you,

67
00:04:16,340 --> 00:04:21,080
he was a bit lacking. His face, his build, you know?

68
00:04:21,510 --> 00:04:24,550
A man who's just tall like a telephone pole...

69
00:04:24,650 --> 00:04:28,290
is bland. Totally useless.

70
00:04:28,690 --> 00:04:32,160
A man should be like our Heung Sik.

71
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:35,660
Sturdy, close to the ground, and dependable.

72
00:04:35,830 --> 00:04:38,300
That's how he doesn't make his family suffer.

73
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:40,630
Isn't that right?

74
00:04:42,830 --> 00:04:47,070
That's right. Right? Oh, our Heung Sik.

75
00:04:47,270 --> 00:04:49,270
Anyone who marries him...

76
00:05:06,790 --> 00:05:08,020
What's that?

77
00:05:08,890 --> 00:05:10,530
The straw Gyeol used.

78
00:05:12,230 --> 00:05:13,660
What are you going to do with that? Seriously...

79
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:15,830
Are you going to get a DNA paternity test?

80
00:05:16,770 --> 00:05:17,770
And then what?

81
00:05:18,070 --> 00:05:20,840
On the off chance he is your son, what will you do?

82
00:05:21,870 --> 00:05:22,870
Exactly.

83
00:05:24,070 --> 00:05:25,310
What should I do?

84
00:05:26,210 --> 00:05:28,410
Are you going to take him away from Gyu Rim?

85
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:30,350
Or what? Try to get back together with her or...

86
00:05:33,450 --> 00:05:35,790
Are you going to make her get a divorce and marry you?

87
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:38,520
No.

88
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:42,960
I don't have the right to do that. What right would I have?

89
00:05:44,230 --> 00:05:45,600
I'm not some stalker.

90
00:05:45,830 --> 00:05:47,860
To suddenly jump into Han Gyu Rim's life...

91
00:05:47,930 --> 00:05:49,300
and turn it upside down...

92
00:05:51,270 --> 00:05:52,500
I don't have that right.

93
00:05:53,670 --> 00:05:55,040
You've come to your senses.

94
00:05:57,740 --> 00:05:58,910
Let's throw this away.

95
00:06:02,810 --> 00:06:03,980
My friend.

96
00:06:04,880 --> 00:06:07,980
You're really back to normal. It's so good to have you back.

97
00:06:08,550 --> 00:06:11,250
Yes, let's stop here.

98
00:06:12,220 --> 00:06:13,490
You made the right choice.

99
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:15,590
Just forget about it completely. Let's forget it.

100
00:06:15,730 --> 00:06:18,400
Han Gyu Rim has the right to forget you, too.

101
00:06:49,690 --> 00:06:51,230
What are you doing alone in the dark?

102
00:06:53,260 --> 00:06:54,430
I'm thinking about something.

103
00:06:56,400 --> 00:06:57,400
About what?

104
00:06:58,100 --> 00:06:59,640
It's just something.

105
00:07:00,870 --> 00:07:03,240
Is it something your uncle can help with or not?

106
00:07:04,240 --> 00:07:05,240
Not.

107
00:07:05,580 --> 00:07:06,910
You won't know unless you tell me.

108
00:07:08,110 --> 00:07:11,080
It's about someone you don't know, Uncle.

109
00:07:12,320 --> 00:07:14,650
No, wait. Maybe you do know him?

110
00:07:14,850 --> 00:07:18,190
- Since you're older than me. - What? Who is it?

111
00:07:19,590 --> 00:07:20,590
Oh, it's nothing.

112
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:22,830
Uncle, never mind me and go study.

113
00:07:23,630 --> 00:07:24,630
All right.

114
00:07:25,230 --> 00:07:26,860
So I'll just mind my own business and study while you...

115
00:07:26,930 --> 00:07:28,430
keep worrying your head off.

116
00:07:32,170 --> 00:07:33,700
You really think I'd do that?

117
00:07:34,900 --> 00:07:36,210
My youngest uncle...

118
00:07:36,270 --> 00:07:38,170
is way too interested in me. It's a problem.

119
00:07:38,740 --> 00:07:40,010
What is it?

120
00:07:43,450 --> 00:07:44,480
Mom's...

121
00:07:44,950 --> 00:07:47,380
The man Mom liked eight years ago showed up.

122
00:07:47,580 --> 00:07:48,590
Eight years ago?

123
00:07:49,120 --> 00:07:50,220
If it was eight years ago...

124
00:07:51,320 --> 00:07:52,460
You mean Mu Jin?

125
00:07:53,060 --> 00:07:54,290
You know him?

126
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:55,690
Of course. When we were little,

127
00:07:55,760 --> 00:07:57,530
he bought Gyu Min and me a lot of snacks,

128
00:07:57,590 --> 00:07:59,000
and we even took sticker photos together.

129
00:07:59,860 --> 00:08:01,530
So Mu Jin showed up again?

130
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:03,630
Where is he now?

131
00:08:03,700 --> 00:08:04,700
Does our oldest sister know?

132
00:08:04,770 --> 00:08:05,840
Did she meet him too?

133
00:08:05,970 --> 00:08:06,970
What did our sister say?

134
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:08,040
She must have been so surprised, right?

135
00:08:10,310 --> 00:08:12,040
The guy our big sister used to date?

136
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:16,980
Who said that?

137
00:08:17,250 --> 00:08:19,950
Gyeol did. They met while playing a game,

138
00:08:20,150 --> 00:08:21,890
and now Gyeol and Mu Jin are best friends.

139
00:08:22,050 --> 00:08:23,650
Where is he now?

140
00:08:24,190 --> 00:08:26,290
Wait, no, does our big sister know?

141
00:08:26,560 --> 00:08:29,530
Did she meet him too? What did she say?

142
00:08:29,590 --> 00:08:31,060
She must have been so surprised, right?

143
00:08:31,490 --> 00:08:32,830
She didn't cry, did she?

144
00:08:33,630 --> 00:08:35,060
You two really are twins.

145
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:39,940
He can't give Gyu Rim a hard time again.

146
00:08:40,700 --> 00:08:42,740
Did Mu Jin give her a hard time?

147
00:08:44,910 --> 00:08:46,110
It's complicated.

148
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:48,580
What do you mean by that?

149
00:08:49,750 --> 00:08:51,550
You're too young to know.

150
00:08:55,190 --> 00:08:56,890
What's Gyu Rim going to do?

151
00:09:06,730 --> 00:09:07,830
Gyu Rim.

152
00:09:09,630 --> 00:09:10,900
Heung Sik?

153
00:09:11,670 --> 00:09:13,270
The owner had business in Majang-dong.

154
00:09:13,340 --> 00:09:15,170
He left work early.

155
00:09:16,410 --> 00:09:19,610
I'm not here to see my mom. I came to see you.

156
00:09:20,510 --> 00:09:21,510
Me?

157
00:09:21,580 --> 00:09:23,650
I felt like I had to tell you something.

158
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:30,020
I fell for Gyeol's trick questions today.

159
00:09:30,450 --> 00:09:32,090
What do you mean?

160
00:09:32,260 --> 00:09:35,360
Well, you see...

161
00:09:36,490 --> 00:09:38,630
That back in the day, you and that guy, Kim Mu Jin,

162
00:09:38,700 --> 00:09:40,200
used to like each other...

163
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:43,630
- Gyeol found out. - What?

164
00:09:44,230 --> 00:09:45,400
No, it's just that Gyeol...

165
00:09:45,470 --> 00:09:47,200
He's so little but he's way too smart...

166
00:09:47,370 --> 00:09:49,370
No, no, it's my mouth. This thing...

167
00:09:50,170 --> 00:09:52,140
My big mouth is the problem.

168
00:09:52,210 --> 00:09:53,780
What am I going to do with this mouth?

169
00:09:55,380 --> 00:09:57,010
I'm so sorry, Gyu Rim.

170
00:10:02,690 --> 00:10:05,790
Did you and my mom like each other?

171
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:16,170
Do you still like her?

172
00:10:34,720 --> 00:10:38,150
Mom, are you mad at me or something?

173
00:10:41,590 --> 00:10:43,890
Why haven't you looked at me since yesterday?

174
00:10:50,530 --> 00:10:52,640
I asked if you're mad at me.

175
00:10:58,210 --> 00:11:00,080
Why are you digging into my past?

176
00:11:01,950 --> 00:11:03,580
Is that why you're mad?

177
00:11:03,810 --> 00:11:05,750
If you were curious, you should have just asked me.

178
00:11:05,920 --> 00:11:07,620
Why did you have to bother Jo Heung Sik?

179
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:10,690
If I asked you, you wouldn't be honest with me.

180
00:11:16,730 --> 00:11:20,860
You knew the Game Man all along, but you lied about it.

181
00:11:29,670 --> 00:11:31,110
You can't stand it when other men show...

182
00:11:31,170 --> 00:11:32,240
the slightest interest in me.

183
00:11:32,310 --> 00:11:34,180
You hated it so much you'd faint.

184
00:11:36,580 --> 00:11:38,210
You even said an actor like Kim Woo Bin...

185
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:39,350
wasn't good enough for me.

186
00:11:39,780 --> 00:11:41,990
- Am I right or wrong? - You're right.

187
00:11:42,050 --> 00:11:44,190
So why are you so nice to the Game Man?

188
00:11:44,820 --> 00:11:46,660
Is it just because he bought you items for your game?

189
00:11:50,890 --> 00:11:53,630
Because I'm sick of not having a dad.

190
00:11:56,330 --> 00:12:01,040
I can't stand it anymore when Cheol Gi brags about his dad,

191
00:12:01,270 --> 00:12:05,710
and I can't take the other kids teasing me for not having one.

192
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:11,080
But the Game Man said he's not interested in you.

193
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:14,620
He said he's not interested in married women.

194
00:12:17,090 --> 00:12:19,860
He's the only man I've ever liked in my entire life,

195
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:21,790
so what am I going to do now?

196
00:13:04,470 --> 00:13:05,470
Darn it.

197
00:13:05,900 --> 00:13:08,400
Seriously. I left just like that,

198
00:13:08,470 --> 00:13:11,270
and not one of them has called, texted, or messaged me?

199
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:12,940
And you call yourselves family?

200
00:13:13,640 --> 00:13:16,880
Fine. Whatever. I'm done too.

201
00:13:17,010 --> 00:13:18,680
I'm completely done with the wretched Han family.

202
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:19,920
Darn it.

203
00:13:21,380 --> 00:13:22,390
I heard...

204
00:13:22,390 --> 00:13:23,990
you asked my husband for help with the wedding ceremony.

205
00:13:25,320 --> 00:13:26,360
That's not happening.

206
00:13:28,020 --> 00:13:29,360
I won't let him go.

207
00:13:33,160 --> 00:13:34,160
Seriously.

208
00:13:35,230 --> 00:13:36,230
Seriously.

209
00:13:58,990 --> 00:14:00,120
Sit down. Make yourself comfortable.

210
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:07,200
Gyu Young, what do you think you're doing?

211
00:14:07,430 --> 00:14:08,530
Please save me, Chairman.

212
00:14:09,230 --> 00:14:10,530
Please just save me one more time.

213
00:14:13,340 --> 00:14:14,370
Get up. Hurry.

214
00:14:14,970 --> 00:14:16,410
If you help me just one more time,

215
00:14:16,810 --> 00:14:19,140
I promise I'll never contact you about anything ever again.

216
00:14:19,710 --> 00:14:22,710
If we pass on the street, I'll walk by like you're a stranger.

217
00:14:22,780 --> 00:14:26,250
Whatever it is, please get up first.

218
00:14:26,450 --> 00:14:28,020
Let's sit down and talk.

219
00:14:29,390 --> 00:14:32,460
I'm not getting up until you give me your word, Chairman.

220
00:14:36,430 --> 00:14:38,090
What is it that I have to promise you?

221
00:14:41,630 --> 00:14:43,770
Please come to my wedding...

222
00:14:44,630 --> 00:14:46,200
just this once. Please.

223
00:14:50,310 --> 00:14:52,940
I was actually about to contact you, Gyu Young.

224
00:14:53,840 --> 00:14:56,050
May I have your future in-laws' contact information?

225
00:14:57,180 --> 00:14:58,280
Why do you need their contact information?

226
00:14:59,150 --> 00:15:01,880
I need to apologise before it's too late.

227
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:04,490
I have to make things right.

228
00:15:04,950 --> 00:15:06,020
That's what we'll do.

229
00:15:06,360 --> 00:15:07,490
Chairman.

230
00:15:07,820 --> 00:15:09,430
After the formal family meeting,

231
00:15:10,090 --> 00:15:12,360
I've felt uneasy and uncomfortable ever since.

232
00:15:13,330 --> 00:15:16,530
Right. I may have gone because I felt I had no choice,

233
00:15:17,470 --> 00:15:20,300
but no matter how I look at it, this just isn't right.

234
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:22,210
So,

235
00:15:23,040 --> 00:15:25,580
I'll meet with your fiance's parents,

236
00:15:25,640 --> 00:15:27,110
explain the situation,

237
00:15:27,640 --> 00:15:28,850
and I will apologise.

238
00:15:30,080 --> 00:15:32,520
How will you explain it, and how will you apologise?

239
00:15:33,650 --> 00:15:34,780
I'll take care of that...

240
00:15:34,850 --> 00:15:36,290
By saying you got duped by a con artist...

241
00:15:36,350 --> 00:15:38,960
and dragged through the mud? You'll clear your conscience...

242
00:15:39,020 --> 00:15:40,560
and wash your hands of the whole thing?

243
00:15:40,860 --> 00:15:42,230
That's not what I meant.

244
00:15:42,360 --> 00:15:43,360
Then what about me?

245
00:15:43,690 --> 00:15:45,090
Do you think my future in-laws will just say, "Oh, okay?"

246
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:46,860
"So that's what happened. We understand completely."

247
00:15:47,030 --> 00:15:48,230
"She must have been desperate..."

248
00:15:49,030 --> 00:15:50,600
Do you think they'll just let it go?

249
00:15:50,670 --> 00:15:51,670
Gyu Young.

250
00:15:52,470 --> 00:15:55,370
It's true that you introduced me as your father.

251
00:15:56,010 --> 00:15:59,210
And yes, having two fathers...

252
00:15:59,580 --> 00:16:01,210
That's not your fault.

253
00:16:02,810 --> 00:16:04,250
So don't worry too much.

254
00:16:05,050 --> 00:16:08,080
If I explain it well, I'm sure they'll understand.

255
00:16:09,820 --> 00:16:12,020
If you're not going to help, then don't ruin everything for me.

256
00:16:14,520 --> 00:16:16,130
- Gyu Young. - If...

257
00:16:17,260 --> 00:16:19,060
If my marriage gets ruined because of you, Chairman,

258
00:16:19,560 --> 00:16:21,060
I won't just sit back and do nothing.

259
00:16:22,530 --> 00:16:24,530
I know whose fault it is my life turned out this way.

260
00:16:25,230 --> 00:16:26,740
She had me just because she felt like it,

261
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:29,840
abandoned her kids to go off and live a good life,

262
00:16:30,610 --> 00:16:32,940
and you think I'm just going to let her get away with it?

263
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:32,400
(Immigration to America)

264
00:17:32,470 --> 00:17:33,840
(Family immigration: A US citizen or resident relative sponsors you.)

265
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:42,680
Are you feeling any better?

266
00:17:43,850 --> 00:17:46,180
You had a fever last night.

267
00:17:47,120 --> 00:17:48,180
I'm fine.

268
00:17:50,050 --> 00:17:51,050
Let me see.

269
00:17:54,160 --> 00:17:55,160
You seem fine.

270
00:17:56,490 --> 00:17:57,990
What are you looking at so intently?

271
00:18:00,400 --> 00:18:01,400
"Immigrating to America."

272
00:18:03,970 --> 00:18:05,630
America's too close. What's a country...

273
00:18:05,700 --> 00:18:06,800
that's even farther away?

274
00:18:07,240 --> 00:18:08,800
Are you really going to emigrate?

275
00:18:09,140 --> 00:18:10,140
Yes.

276
00:18:13,940 --> 00:18:16,480
Why? Is it because of Mu Jin?

277
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:19,520
A man who doesn't even see me as a woman...

278
00:18:19,580 --> 00:18:22,020
I'm tired of this 23-year crush,

279
00:18:22,520 --> 00:18:23,520
and I think it's best if I leave...

280
00:18:23,590 --> 00:18:24,950
so I don't have to see any of this.

281
00:18:26,960 --> 00:18:30,090
I really hate Han Gyu Rim, but I'm also really envious of her.

282
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:33,930
Who?

283
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,030
Who did you say?

284
00:18:36,570 --> 00:18:37,570
Han Gyu Rim.

285
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:39,870
The woman with Mu Jin. Her name is Han Gyu Rim.

286
00:18:43,510 --> 00:18:45,570
Why? Do you know her?

287
00:18:46,210 --> 00:18:47,340
Oh, no.

288
00:18:48,980 --> 00:18:51,210
Her age? How old is she?

289
00:18:52,210 --> 00:18:53,320
I think she's my age.

290
00:18:56,620 --> 00:18:57,620
Where does she...

291
00:18:59,320 --> 00:19:00,790
What neighbourhood does she live in?

292
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:02,690
I don't know.

293
00:19:03,590 --> 00:19:06,160
Why? Are you going to track her down and rip her hair out?

294
00:19:11,970 --> 00:19:14,940
For the 7 items, that's 23 dollars total.

295
00:19:15,500 --> 00:19:17,170
The potato salad is on the house.

296
00:19:17,240 --> 00:19:18,240
Thank you.

297
00:19:19,710 --> 00:19:20,710
Thank you.

298
00:19:25,450 --> 00:19:28,920
You must be mother and daughter. You two look so much alike.

299
00:19:30,190 --> 00:19:33,520
- Here you go. - No way. I'm way prettier.

300
00:19:33,590 --> 00:19:34,860
Oh, honestly.

301
00:19:35,890 --> 00:19:37,860
- Hope business goes well. - Thank you. Goodbye.

302
00:19:38,660 --> 00:19:41,130
- Best place. And we got a freebie. - It looks delicious.

303
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:43,470
- Let's come again. Looks delicious. - Yes.

304
00:19:47,200 --> 00:19:48,200
Are you jealous?

305
00:19:49,140 --> 00:19:50,140
No.

306
00:19:50,910 --> 00:19:52,680
Don't you miss your mom?

307
00:19:54,940 --> 00:19:57,380
Your mother is really something.

308
00:19:58,280 --> 00:19:59,750
Even if she remarried,

309
00:19:59,820 --> 00:20:02,320
you'd think she'd visit at least once.

310
00:20:03,550 --> 00:20:04,990
As long as she's living well, that's all that matters.

311
00:20:06,220 --> 00:20:07,890
Were there any delivery orders today?

312
00:20:08,690 --> 00:20:12,630
Are you kidding? We're swamped. There's a long list. Go on, hurry.

313
00:20:13,560 --> 00:20:15,000
Let's trim these scallions, all right?

314
00:20:17,900 --> 00:20:20,100
How was that recipe I sent you last time?

315
00:20:21,170 --> 00:20:22,440
Was it good?

316
00:20:23,110 --> 00:20:24,270
Did people like it?

317
00:20:27,240 --> 00:20:29,280
Nice, good to hear that.

318
00:20:30,750 --> 00:20:34,620
Your recipe? I told you. It was awesome.

319
00:20:40,290 --> 00:20:41,290
Okay.

320
00:20:42,890 --> 00:20:44,930
Okay, see you.

321
00:20:47,360 --> 00:20:50,430
Suragan's was way better. Why are we back to Mom's?

322
00:20:50,570 --> 00:20:52,470
I know, right? According to the reviews,

323
00:20:52,540 --> 00:20:54,500
their greens and side dishes are the best.

324
00:20:54,570 --> 00:20:56,510
And they say the pancakes and stews are even more incredible.

325
00:20:56,570 --> 00:20:57,570
Hey.

326
00:20:57,640 --> 00:20:59,070
The boss told us never to order from Suragan,

327
00:20:59,140 --> 00:21:00,140
so what are we supposed to do?

328
00:21:00,440 --> 00:21:03,280
He wanted to repackage their food and sell it as our own.

329
00:21:03,980 --> 00:21:06,680
I think there's something going on between the boss and Mom's.

330
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:09,120
Why? Is he taking bribes?

331
00:21:10,120 --> 00:21:11,520
No. That's not it.

332
00:21:13,490 --> 00:21:14,660
What are they talking about?

333
00:21:14,760 --> 00:21:16,530
What? And what's Suragan?

334
00:21:16,830 --> 00:21:17,890
Well...

335
00:21:17,960 --> 00:21:19,960
There's a side dish shop we recently found.

336
00:21:20,030 --> 00:21:21,460
Their side dishes are amazing, so...

337
00:21:21,530 --> 00:21:23,930
- the staff absolutely loved them. - Yes.

338
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:25,000
But the boss...

339
00:21:25,070 --> 00:21:26,270
suddenly told us that we're absolutely...

340
00:21:26,340 --> 00:21:27,340
not allowed to order from there.

341
00:21:27,400 --> 00:21:28,440
Why not?

342
00:21:28,840 --> 00:21:31,440
Isn't that the place you were all raving about,

343
00:21:31,510 --> 00:21:33,180
the one I wanted to try?

344
00:21:33,380 --> 00:21:34,380
Yes.

345
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:36,350
Is it really that good?

346
00:21:36,350 --> 00:21:37,550
- It's incredible. - It's incredible.

347
00:21:37,680 --> 00:21:39,350
Chef, you really have to try it.

348
00:21:40,820 --> 00:21:42,280
We have some leftover Suragan side dishes...

349
00:21:42,350 --> 00:21:43,890
in the fridge. Would you like to try some?

350
00:21:43,950 --> 00:21:44,950
Okay, bring them over.

351
00:21:45,020 --> 00:21:46,020
Yes, sir.

352
00:21:46,460 --> 00:21:48,960
If there's corruption, we should just fire him.

353
00:21:49,020 --> 00:21:50,030
The boss?

354
00:21:50,090 --> 00:21:51,430
What's the big deal if he's the boss?

355
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:55,060
You guys just have to rise up. For our one staff meal a day,

356
00:21:55,130 --> 00:21:57,400
say, "We want to eat the side dishes we want."

357
00:21:57,530 --> 00:21:58,530
Chef.

358
00:21:58,600 --> 00:21:59,900
Have you considered a career in politics?

359
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:01,500
However, if the side dishes aren't good,

360
00:22:01,570 --> 00:22:02,570
I'm going to fire you all.

361
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:04,270
For the crime of falsely accusing the boss.

362
00:22:04,340 --> 00:22:06,210
- Yes, we're confident. - Of course.

363
00:22:06,910 --> 00:22:07,910
Chef.

364
00:22:08,710 --> 00:22:09,780
Have a taste.

365
00:22:09,780 --> 00:22:11,450
- This is it? - Yes.

366
00:22:14,750 --> 00:22:16,920
Is this the kimchi?

367
00:22:34,870 --> 00:22:36,310
Wow, this is good.

368
00:22:37,640 --> 00:22:39,210
This is really good.

369
00:22:39,710 --> 00:22:40,940
Where did you guys find this place?

370
00:22:41,240 --> 00:22:42,380
It was nothing.

371
00:22:43,680 --> 00:22:46,020
- Where's Park Jung Woo right now? - He's in his office.

372
00:22:46,120 --> 00:22:47,120
That jerk.

373
00:22:52,490 --> 00:22:53,490
Mr. CEO,

374
00:22:54,220 --> 00:22:55,620
you should leave your post immediately.

375
00:22:56,060 --> 00:22:57,560
The people are staging an uprising.

376
00:22:57,760 --> 00:22:58,960
What are you talking about?

377
00:22:59,190 --> 00:23:00,200
Hey, you.

378
00:23:00,260 --> 00:23:02,430
Why won't you let us switch to the side dish place...

379
00:23:02,500 --> 00:23:03,800
that most of the staff says is delicious?

380
00:23:04,170 --> 00:23:05,230
What is this, a dictatorship?

381
00:23:05,300 --> 00:23:06,300
What place...

382
00:23:08,370 --> 00:23:09,810
Suragan?

383
00:23:11,010 --> 00:23:12,210
That place is terrible.

384
00:23:12,510 --> 00:23:15,140
Hey, you're the one who raved about how great that place was.

385
00:23:15,680 --> 00:23:16,810
After eating there for a while,

386
00:23:16,880 --> 00:23:18,250
I realised they just load it with MSG,

387
00:23:18,310 --> 00:23:19,550
so it's not healthy.

388
00:23:19,980 --> 00:23:22,950
Well, I just tried it, and I couldn't taste any MSG at all.

389
00:23:24,920 --> 00:23:26,790
The owner is rude.

390
00:23:27,160 --> 00:23:28,790
Now that they're popular, they don't give you any extras,

391
00:23:28,860 --> 00:23:30,390
and I think they're skimping on the portions.

392
00:23:30,460 --> 00:23:31,460
For the same price,

393
00:23:31,530 --> 00:23:32,530
Mom's gives double the amount.

394
00:23:33,160 --> 00:23:34,430
Really?

395
00:23:36,470 --> 00:23:39,670
- I should go check it out myself. - Freeze.

396
00:23:40,200 --> 00:23:42,400
Hey, why are you going there?

397
00:23:42,500 --> 00:23:43,770
Do you have nothing better to do?

398
00:23:45,810 --> 00:23:48,940
- This is getting suspicious. - What's so suspicious?

399
00:23:50,210 --> 00:23:51,310
Move.

400
00:23:52,350 --> 00:23:53,820
Don't you trust me?

401
00:23:54,450 --> 00:23:55,980
Do I have to get your permission...

402
00:23:56,050 --> 00:23:57,090
for everything, even their side dishes?

403
00:23:57,150 --> 00:23:59,250
If that's the case, then you be the CEO, you jerk.

404
00:23:59,890 --> 00:24:00,890
Hey, you know you're being really weird...

405
00:24:00,960 --> 00:24:03,560
- today, right? - I don't know. What's so weird?

406
00:24:03,960 --> 00:24:05,060
If I knew it all, would I work under you...

407
00:24:05,130 --> 00:24:06,830
as your second-rate CEO?

408
00:24:07,660 --> 00:24:09,370
What are you even talking about?

409
00:24:10,370 --> 00:24:11,570
Move already.

410
00:24:11,900 --> 00:24:13,340
Seriously, don't go.

411
00:24:14,600 --> 00:24:15,840
Seriously?

412
00:24:21,710 --> 00:24:22,980
What is that smell?

413
00:24:38,160 --> 00:24:39,930
- What are you doing? - Oh, hey...

414
00:24:40,230 --> 00:24:41,700
You're awake?

415
00:24:42,900 --> 00:24:45,430
I was trying to make you your favourite sweet potato fries.

416
00:24:48,840 --> 00:24:49,870
It's hot.

417
00:24:50,310 --> 00:24:53,940
Move, move. You never do this kind of thing.

418
00:24:54,040 --> 00:24:55,040
Come here.

419
00:24:56,010 --> 00:24:58,710
I was just trying to make them really delicious for you.

420
00:25:00,350 --> 00:25:02,350
Gyu Oh, you like sweet potato fries, don't you?

421
00:25:02,550 --> 00:25:03,820
No, I don't.

422
00:25:04,590 --> 00:25:07,860
You used to go crazy for sweet potato fries.

423
00:25:09,530 --> 00:25:10,530
Just go sit down.

424
00:25:12,430 --> 00:25:14,230
That must be Gyu Young.

425
00:25:16,900 --> 00:25:18,130
Then was it potatoes?

426
00:25:18,930 --> 00:25:21,040
Should I buy some potatoes and make you French fries?

427
00:25:21,100 --> 00:25:22,640
I don't like potatoes either.

428
00:25:23,170 --> 00:25:24,910
Oh, right. Then...

429
00:25:25,270 --> 00:25:26,340
Corn?

430
00:25:27,980 --> 00:25:30,650
What? Carrots...

431
00:25:31,180 --> 00:25:33,020
Cucumbers, onions...

432
00:25:33,080 --> 00:25:34,280
What should I make you?

433
00:25:38,520 --> 00:25:39,520
Do you need money again?

434
00:25:40,590 --> 00:25:42,560
Hey, what kind of father do you take me for?

435
00:25:43,430 --> 00:25:47,460
Hey, I'm really doing this for you, you know? I even burned my arm.

436
00:25:47,530 --> 00:25:48,600
I was trying to make something you like,

437
00:25:48,660 --> 00:25:52,400
and earlier, I even cut my finger slicing sweet potatoes.

438
00:25:53,600 --> 00:25:54,770
Exactly.

439
00:25:55,070 --> 00:25:56,410
Why are you acting so strange all of a sudden?

440
00:25:56,810 --> 00:25:59,270
No, it's not all of a sudden.

441
00:25:59,980 --> 00:26:03,480
I've always had it in me. You just don't know it,

442
00:26:03,580 --> 00:26:06,720
but I'm surprisingly a very affectionate father.

443
00:26:08,150 --> 00:26:09,180
Are you sick or something?

444
00:26:09,750 --> 00:26:11,690
Are you planning on dying soon?

445
00:26:12,120 --> 00:26:15,790
Gosh, the things you say.

446
00:26:20,760 --> 00:26:22,930
After I saw the kids fighting yesterday,

447
00:26:24,400 --> 00:26:26,940
I couldn't get a wink of sleep all night.

448
00:26:28,540 --> 00:26:30,640
I took a long, hard look at the life I've lived so far,

449
00:26:30,910 --> 00:26:33,540
and I just thought it over carefully,

450
00:26:35,040 --> 00:26:37,180
and it's all my fault.

451
00:26:37,910 --> 00:26:39,250
I'm the one to blame.

452
00:26:40,150 --> 00:26:41,780
To all of you,

453
00:26:42,220 --> 00:26:43,920
I failed to be a proper father.

454
00:26:44,590 --> 00:26:46,150
So from now on,

455
00:26:46,220 --> 00:26:48,120
all the things I failed to do for you,

456
00:26:48,190 --> 00:26:50,260
all the things I neglected, I'm going to do every one of them...

457
00:26:51,230 --> 00:26:53,360
and take some time to repent.

458
00:26:53,430 --> 00:26:56,370
You've never had a single thought like that in your entire life,

459
00:26:57,500 --> 00:26:59,000
and now all of a sudden you're thinking this way?

460
00:26:59,430 --> 00:27:01,370
Father, are you sure you're not seriously sick?

461
00:27:01,940 --> 00:27:03,940
They say a sudden change in a person means they're about to die.

462
00:27:05,440 --> 00:27:08,640
You really don't quit, do you? Why?

463
00:27:08,710 --> 00:27:10,810
Do you want your father to get seriously sick...

464
00:27:10,880 --> 00:27:12,450
and just drop dead?

465
00:27:13,220 --> 00:27:16,750
Just go back to how you were. Stop making people worry.

466
00:27:18,020 --> 00:27:19,020
Hey, my eldest son.

467
00:27:24,830 --> 00:27:25,990
You want me...

468
00:27:28,130 --> 00:27:30,230
to go back to how I was?

469
00:27:31,270 --> 00:27:32,270
Is that what you want?

470
00:27:32,870 --> 00:27:34,300
What is he talking about now?

471
00:27:38,910 --> 00:27:39,910
Son.

472
00:27:40,610 --> 00:27:41,910
Of course.

473
00:27:41,980 --> 00:27:45,950
You really are my eldest son. You're a good kid.

474
00:27:48,080 --> 00:27:49,690
Hey, hey, you got something on you.

475
00:27:51,990 --> 00:27:53,290
My good eldest son.

476
00:27:54,060 --> 00:27:57,130
Gyu Young, the twins, and the others,

477
00:27:57,690 --> 00:27:59,700
they're all asking when I'm finally going to grow up.

478
00:27:59,760 --> 00:28:02,100
They tell me to get my act together and live a proper life, you know?

479
00:28:02,260 --> 00:28:04,500
They nag and yell at me,

480
00:28:04,570 --> 00:28:06,170
and they're just dying to give me a hard time.

481
00:28:07,470 --> 00:28:09,300
But my eldest son here...

482
00:28:09,470 --> 00:28:12,710
You're saying you understand and accept your father, right?

483
00:28:12,770 --> 00:28:13,780
Well...

484
00:28:14,480 --> 00:28:17,650
Thank you, Gyu Oh. You...

485
00:28:17,880 --> 00:28:20,820
You were special to me from the day you were born.

486
00:28:20,880 --> 00:28:21,880
You know?

487
00:28:23,590 --> 00:28:25,220
You're the only one I have.

488
00:28:27,190 --> 00:28:28,920
- Just stay still. - Let go of me. I...

489
00:28:28,990 --> 00:28:31,490
Stay still, you punk. Let me give you a hug.

490
00:28:37,230 --> 00:28:39,200
(456 Geumje-dong 4ga)

491
00:28:53,580 --> 00:28:54,620
You know who I am, right?

492
00:28:55,420 --> 00:28:58,050
- No, I don't. - You really don't?

493
00:28:58,790 --> 00:29:01,290
I said I don't know you. Who are you?

494
00:29:12,500 --> 00:29:13,600
Welcome...

495
00:29:14,600 --> 00:29:16,170
What is it this time?

496
00:29:16,240 --> 00:29:18,510
Did your sister forget something again?

497
00:29:19,510 --> 00:29:20,740
No, it's not that.

498
00:29:22,880 --> 00:29:24,880
There's something I wanted to ask you.

499
00:29:25,080 --> 00:29:26,920
Me? What is it?

500
00:29:30,390 --> 00:29:32,120
The last time I was here at the shop,

501
00:29:32,190 --> 00:29:34,090
a young woman came in, remember?

502
00:29:34,690 --> 00:29:37,630
I get plenty of young women in here.

503
00:29:38,160 --> 00:29:39,860
It seemed like you knew her well.

504
00:29:41,100 --> 00:29:43,430
I know a lot of people.

505
00:29:46,370 --> 00:29:48,070
She was wearing a light blue dress,

506
00:29:48,140 --> 00:29:50,570
and she had big eyes and a cute face.

507
00:29:51,670 --> 00:29:54,240
Oh, she's the one who used to come to your old food stall.

508
00:29:54,710 --> 00:29:56,180
Oh, you mean Hee Na.

509
00:29:56,240 --> 00:29:58,810
- You must mean Hee Na. - Yes, that's her.

510
00:29:59,050 --> 00:30:01,020
But why are you asking about Hee Na?

511
00:30:02,950 --> 00:30:03,950
Why?

512
00:30:04,390 --> 00:30:06,250
Could I possibly get her contact information?

513
00:30:07,860 --> 00:30:10,030
She did leave her phone number.

514
00:30:10,930 --> 00:30:14,730
But I can't just give it out to anyone, can I?

515
00:30:15,860 --> 00:30:19,100
Well, I mean, of course you're not just anyone, Gyu Oh.

516
00:30:19,330 --> 00:30:22,370
Right? I can vouch for who you are.

517
00:30:23,110 --> 00:30:24,970
Still, though...

518
00:30:25,110 --> 00:30:27,510
I promise I won't cause any trouble for you.

519
00:30:27,640 --> 00:30:28,710
I just need to ask her one single thing.

520
00:30:29,480 --> 00:30:30,480
What is it?

521
00:30:30,650 --> 00:30:32,510
What are you going to ask her?

522
00:30:35,580 --> 00:30:37,350
What is it? Go on and tell me.

523
00:30:38,090 --> 00:30:40,490
Oh my goodness, I'm dying of curiosity now.

524
00:30:41,220 --> 00:30:42,260
Should I tell you?

525
00:30:42,260 --> 00:30:44,290
All right, that's all for today.

526
00:30:44,460 --> 00:30:47,160
Wash hands and enjoy your meal.

527
00:30:47,160 --> 00:30:48,830
- Okay. - Okay.

528
00:30:48,900 --> 00:30:50,070
Don't be a picky eater.

529
00:30:50,130 --> 00:30:52,030
Try to eat a little bit of everything.

530
00:30:52,100 --> 00:30:54,200
Okay.

531
00:31:04,350 --> 00:31:05,510
(Min Ju)

532
00:31:05,580 --> 00:31:07,980
In class? Big news, big news.

533
00:31:08,280 --> 00:31:09,620
Call me as soon as you're done, please.

534
00:31:15,820 --> 00:31:16,830
What big news?

535
00:31:17,190 --> 00:31:18,190
Kwon Hee Na.

536
00:31:18,390 --> 00:31:20,230
That bastard is finally out of the picture.

537
00:31:20,960 --> 00:31:21,960
Really?

538
00:31:22,030 --> 00:31:23,770
Yes. Apparently, the Gigolo told my mom...

539
00:31:23,830 --> 00:31:25,670
they should break up and then ghosted her.

540
00:31:26,430 --> 00:31:27,440
Wow.

541
00:31:28,470 --> 00:31:30,110
Is your mom okay?

542
00:31:30,540 --> 00:31:31,970
Of course she's not okay.

543
00:31:32,570 --> 00:31:33,580
She's a complete mess,

544
00:31:33,640 --> 00:31:34,910
crying her eyes out behind our backs.

545
00:31:35,310 --> 00:31:37,580
But anyway, that's a good thing, right?

546
00:31:38,180 --> 00:31:39,180
It's a very good thing.

547
00:31:39,780 --> 00:31:41,020
It's all thanks to you, Hee Na.

548
00:31:41,350 --> 00:31:44,050
I'll treat you to a nice dinner or drinks soon, my treat.

549
00:31:44,690 --> 00:31:46,120
Okay, talk to you soon.

550
00:31:56,600 --> 00:31:57,600
(Gigolo)

551
00:31:57,670 --> 00:31:58,830
(Gigolo Bastard)

552
00:31:59,130 --> 00:32:02,140
He gets the message loud and clear. He's not stupid.

553
00:32:04,040 --> 00:32:06,470
Don't ever come back from Gangnam, you Gigolo.

554
00:32:07,380 --> 00:32:09,240
You're permanently deleted.

555
00:32:09,340 --> 00:32:10,680
(Move This Contact To Trash?)

556
00:32:10,750 --> 00:32:11,750
(Gigolo Bastard)

557
00:32:12,880 --> 00:32:14,950
What the? Why is he calling me?

558
00:32:15,050 --> 00:32:16,050
Darn it.

559
00:32:19,290 --> 00:32:20,290
What is this?

560
00:32:31,430 --> 00:32:33,840
(Kwon Hee Na)

561
00:32:38,810 --> 00:32:41,310
Kwon Hee Na. This is Han Gyu Oh.

562
00:32:41,810 --> 00:32:43,040
Do you really not remember me?

563
00:32:43,750 --> 00:32:45,380
I recognised you the moment I saw you.

564
00:32:47,550 --> 00:32:49,150
(Kwon Hee Na, it's Gyu Oh. Remember? I recognised you at once.)

565
00:33:08,600 --> 00:33:10,540
Why would that jerk call me?

566
00:33:12,570 --> 00:33:14,810
Is he trying to get revenge because I ruined his scam?

567
00:33:16,580 --> 00:33:19,610
Darn it. That's why I made sure to only use pay phones.

568
00:33:21,980 --> 00:33:23,080
Or could it be...

569
00:33:24,020 --> 00:33:25,290
Did he already have my number?

570
00:33:26,590 --> 00:33:28,960
Oh, gosh. What do I do?

571
00:33:31,690 --> 00:33:32,790
I'm sorry, Chef.

572
00:33:34,300 --> 00:33:36,130
I should have checked more carefully.

573
00:33:37,600 --> 00:33:39,700
I did think it wasn't as cold as usual.

574
00:33:40,440 --> 00:33:42,740
But the light was on, so I never thought it was broken.

575
00:33:55,420 --> 00:33:56,420
This is no good.

576
00:33:58,150 --> 00:33:59,590
The problem is dinner service tonight, right?

577
00:34:00,360 --> 00:34:01,360
Yes.

578
00:34:01,420 --> 00:34:03,530
What if we just serve without pickles for tonight...

579
00:34:04,360 --> 00:34:05,360
What?

580
00:34:05,860 --> 00:34:06,860
That won't work, right?

581
00:34:14,670 --> 00:34:15,670
White Kimchi.

582
00:34:18,510 --> 00:34:19,540
That stuff from Suragan earlier.

583
00:34:20,010 --> 00:34:21,010
There's still some of that White Kimchi...

584
00:34:21,080 --> 00:34:22,080
you were eating left, right?

585
00:34:22,140 --> 00:34:24,010
- Yes, we have some. - Bring it to me.

586
00:34:42,800 --> 00:34:43,800
We'll use this.

587
00:34:44,230 --> 00:34:45,230
Well...

588
00:34:45,330 --> 00:34:47,870
But the CEO told us not to order from Suragan...

589
00:34:49,400 --> 00:34:50,640
Unlike that jerk,

590
00:34:51,240 --> 00:34:52,970
I own one percent more of this restaurant than he does.

591
00:34:54,340 --> 00:34:55,340
Okay, where is this place?

592
00:34:55,940 --> 00:34:56,950
I'll find out right away.

593
00:34:58,010 --> 00:34:59,350
(Suragan Side Dishes)

594
00:34:59,480 --> 00:35:00,750
Welcome.

595
00:35:12,690 --> 00:35:14,630
So this is why that bastard Jung Woo told me not to come here.

596
00:35:18,330 --> 00:35:19,570
What are you doing here?

597
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:22,040
I'm here to buy some side dishes.

598
00:35:26,140 --> 00:35:27,410
(Weekly Meal Plan)

599
00:35:28,080 --> 00:35:30,810
Is this all the White Kimchi and Radish Water Kimchi you have?

600
00:35:31,780 --> 00:35:34,480
We have more in another fridge, but it's not ready yet.

601
00:35:35,580 --> 00:35:36,580
I see.

602
00:35:41,320 --> 00:35:43,120
I'm the chef at the restaurant down the street.

603
00:35:43,790 --> 00:35:46,590
Our pickle fridge suddenly broke down,

604
00:35:46,760 --> 00:35:48,300
so we can't use any of the pickles we made.

605
00:35:50,300 --> 00:35:51,300
And?

606
00:35:54,700 --> 00:35:56,200
I'd like to serve the White Kimchi...

607
00:35:56,270 --> 00:35:57,810
and Radish Water Kimchi instead of pickles,

608
00:35:58,540 --> 00:36:00,680
so can I buy everything you have?

609
00:36:02,310 --> 00:36:03,750
I'm sorry, but I can't do that.

610
00:36:05,280 --> 00:36:06,280
Why not?

611
00:36:07,420 --> 00:36:09,550
Some of it is reserved for other customers' pre-orders,

612
00:36:09,850 --> 00:36:11,150
and since the owner isn't here,

613
00:36:11,220 --> 00:36:12,790
I can't make that decision on my own.

614
00:36:13,290 --> 00:36:15,460
So you're not the owner.

615
00:36:16,660 --> 00:36:18,590
What you have out in the store now isn't for pre-orders, right?

616
00:36:19,260 --> 00:36:20,500
Then sell all of that to me.

617
00:36:22,400 --> 00:36:23,870
Just buy it from another store.

618
00:36:24,830 --> 00:36:25,830
Just sell it to me.

619
00:36:26,600 --> 00:36:28,340
I'm not selling it. Please leave.

620
00:36:28,400 --> 00:36:30,710
Why not? Isn't it for sale?

621
00:36:31,710 --> 00:36:33,070
I'm not selling it to you.

622
00:36:33,740 --> 00:36:34,740
Just leave.

623
00:36:34,810 --> 00:36:37,550
Why won't you sell it to me? I'm a paying customer.

624
00:36:38,210 --> 00:36:40,120
I have the right to refuse service to a customer I don't want.

625
00:36:40,520 --> 00:36:41,650
Please leave.

626
00:36:41,780 --> 00:36:46,750
Why don't you want to sell to me? Is there something wrong with me?

627
00:36:54,400 --> 00:36:56,530
Go, before other customers arrive.

628
00:36:57,400 --> 00:37:00,400
I don't care if other customers come or not.

629
00:37:00,870 --> 00:37:03,740
Give me one good reason why you won't sell to me. Just one.

630
00:37:03,910 --> 00:37:04,910
Look here.

631
00:37:04,970 --> 00:37:06,170
Then don't make food that's so...

632
00:37:08,510 --> 00:37:12,250
Don't make it so delicious. You've ruined everyone's palate.

633
00:37:12,310 --> 00:37:13,450
Take responsibility.

634
00:37:22,690 --> 00:37:24,860
Why did you chug the whole glass of wine?

635
00:37:26,360 --> 00:37:28,460
I was just thirsty.

636
00:37:28,800 --> 00:37:31,530
Still, you shouldn't do that. The guests aren't even here yet.

637
00:37:32,600 --> 00:37:34,100
If my mother saw you,

638
00:37:34,170 --> 00:37:36,000
she'd hate it and say you have no class.

639
00:37:38,710 --> 00:37:42,310
I was so drained from dealing with a difficult patient at the hospital.

640
00:37:42,480 --> 00:37:43,950
I was just frustrated.

641
00:37:44,810 --> 00:37:45,810
By the way, who is this person...

642
00:37:45,880 --> 00:37:46,980
that you set up a special dinner for?

643
00:37:47,350 --> 00:37:48,950
You must be really close with him.

644
00:37:49,780 --> 00:37:53,020
Well, we're not super close just yet,

645
00:37:53,660 --> 00:37:55,260
but he's someone I want to be...

646
00:37:55,320 --> 00:37:57,530
good friends with for a very long time.

647
00:37:58,130 --> 00:37:59,130
Is he that important?

648
00:37:59,790 --> 00:38:03,330
If you speak that highly of him, I'd better make a good impression.

649
00:38:03,630 --> 00:38:05,030
Yes, you should.

650
00:38:05,200 --> 00:38:08,670
He's very particular about people,

651
00:38:08,840 --> 00:38:10,710
so don't get on his bad side, okay?

652
00:38:12,010 --> 00:38:13,440
What kind of person is he?

653
00:38:14,010 --> 00:38:15,710
Just how amazing can he be?

654
00:38:16,180 --> 00:38:18,080
Well now, you're here already?

655
00:38:18,650 --> 00:38:21,080
- I tried to get here early. - Hey, you made it.

656
00:38:21,150 --> 00:38:22,150
Hey, Captain.

657
00:38:23,020 --> 00:38:27,320
Wow, I heard you're getting married. You're practically glowing.

658
00:38:28,160 --> 00:38:29,490
I've been getting a lot of treatments lately.

659
00:38:29,560 --> 00:38:30,990
Wow, you look really great.

660
00:38:32,490 --> 00:38:33,760
Is that the woman you're marrying?

661
00:38:34,360 --> 00:38:36,530
Honey, say hello.

662
00:38:36,600 --> 00:38:37,800
This is Heung Sik.

663
00:38:40,100 --> 00:38:41,140
Hello.

664
00:38:41,840 --> 00:38:43,270
How do you do?

665
00:38:43,570 --> 00:38:45,240
Sung Wook has told me a lot about you.

666
00:38:45,940 --> 00:38:46,940
Yes.

667
00:38:49,540 --> 00:38:50,950
What are you doing, honey?

668
00:38:51,010 --> 00:38:52,350
Introduce yourself properly.

669
00:38:53,950 --> 00:38:57,590
It's a pleasure to meet you. My name is Han Gyu Young.

670
00:38:59,750 --> 00:39:00,760
What is it?

671
00:39:01,490 --> 00:39:02,490
Do you know her?

672
00:39:03,960 --> 00:39:08,130
You look an awful lot like someone I know.

673
00:39:08,360 --> 00:39:09,360
What?

674
00:39:10,130 --> 00:39:11,270
It's a pleasure to meet you.

675
00:39:11,770 --> 00:39:13,770
My name is Jo Heung Sik.

676
00:39:15,740 --> 00:39:16,740
No.

677
00:39:17,340 --> 00:39:19,870
Wait, looking closely, you are the person I know.

678
00:39:23,440 --> 00:39:26,150
But on second thought, you're definitely someone else.

679
00:39:26,880 --> 00:39:28,280
- Let's sit. - Okay.

680
00:39:31,390 --> 00:39:33,520
Some wine over here, please.

681
00:39:37,490 --> 00:39:39,890
All right. Everyone, cheers.

682
00:39:52,040 --> 00:39:56,040
Wow, this wine is killer. It's really good.

683
00:39:57,550 --> 00:39:58,650
But hey,

684
00:39:59,250 --> 00:40:01,520
your fiancee is very quiet.

685
00:40:02,120 --> 00:40:03,420
She's not feeling sick, is she?

686
00:40:04,850 --> 00:40:06,490
No, I'm not.

687
00:40:06,920 --> 00:40:07,920
I know.

688
00:40:08,660 --> 00:40:10,090
You've been strangely quiet today, honey.

689
00:40:12,130 --> 00:40:13,800
I told her she had to make a good impression on you,

690
00:40:13,860 --> 00:40:15,630
so I guess this is the concept she's going for.

691
00:40:17,030 --> 00:40:19,200
It's okay, honey. Go on, say something.

692
00:40:23,340 --> 00:40:26,470
So, how did you two meet?

693
00:40:26,970 --> 00:40:28,280
From what I can see, you have nothing in common...

694
00:40:29,210 --> 00:40:30,450
or so it seems.

695
00:40:31,750 --> 00:40:34,320
Let's see. When was that?

696
00:40:34,720 --> 00:40:35,720
Hey, when we first met,

697
00:40:35,780 --> 00:40:37,020
was it 3 years ago? Or 4?

698
00:40:37,650 --> 00:40:40,220
Oh, it was four years ago.

699
00:40:40,520 --> 00:40:41,620
Four years.

700
00:40:42,320 --> 00:40:43,320
Well,

701
00:40:43,590 --> 00:40:45,860
a guy I was in the army with kept asking me to come,

702
00:40:46,160 --> 00:40:47,630
so I went to a yacht race to cheer him on.

703
00:40:48,500 --> 00:40:53,030
And that's where Heung Sik here pulled off a really impressive win.

704
00:40:53,600 --> 00:40:55,600
Before that, I wasn't really interested in yachts...

705
00:40:55,670 --> 00:40:57,000
or anything like that.

706
00:40:57,270 --> 00:40:59,710
But I was so impressed watching him that day...

707
00:40:59,870 --> 00:41:01,140
I went right up to him...

708
00:41:01,210 --> 00:41:02,440
and joined his yacht club on the spot.

709
00:41:03,580 --> 00:41:04,580
Gosh, come on.

710
00:41:04,710 --> 00:41:06,280
I just got lucky that day.

711
00:41:07,480 --> 00:41:08,480
That's why this...

712
00:41:09,320 --> 00:41:11,620
Wait, he competed in a yacht race...

713
00:41:12,150 --> 00:41:14,660
and actually won?

714
00:41:15,360 --> 00:41:16,360
For real?

715
00:41:17,790 --> 00:41:18,790
Why?

716
00:41:20,190 --> 00:41:22,630
What, I don't look like the type to be on a yacht?

717
00:41:25,530 --> 00:41:27,030
Gyu Young, what's with you?

718
00:41:28,400 --> 00:41:31,610
No, it's not that. I was just surprised, that's all.

719
00:41:32,770 --> 00:41:35,510
Just by looking at me, you can tell I look like a rice thief.

720
00:41:35,840 --> 00:41:38,180
So what business do I have on a yacht, right?

721
00:41:38,610 --> 00:41:39,880
It's pretty surprising, isn't it?

722
00:41:40,250 --> 00:41:41,750
No, that's not what I meant.

723
00:41:42,180 --> 00:41:43,990
Why are you being like this too?

724
00:41:44,290 --> 00:41:46,350
Why are you bringing up the "rice thief" thing?

725
00:41:46,820 --> 00:41:48,060
Well...

726
00:41:48,290 --> 00:41:50,930
There's this young woman I know,

727
00:41:52,260 --> 00:41:55,300
and every time she sees me, she calls me a rice thief.

728
00:41:57,130 --> 00:41:58,470
Do I look like one to you too?

729
00:41:59,270 --> 00:42:01,370
To a great guy like you,

730
00:42:01,440 --> 00:42:02,940
how could someone say something so awful?

731
00:42:03,140 --> 00:42:05,210
- That... - Who is she?

732
00:42:05,440 --> 00:42:07,910
What kind of disrespectful brat would say something like that?

733
00:42:09,440 --> 00:42:10,750
In your eyes,

734
00:42:11,610 --> 00:42:13,650
do I look like a rice thief?

735
00:42:14,420 --> 00:42:15,420
No.

736
00:42:16,020 --> 00:42:17,590
There must be something wrong with her eyes.

737
00:42:17,590 --> 00:42:18,820
Right?

738
00:42:18,820 --> 00:42:21,890
- Something's wrong with her eyes. - Exactly.

739
00:42:22,560 --> 00:42:26,760
So? You just let a brat like that get away with it?

740
00:42:28,030 --> 00:42:29,260
Well, what else am I supposed to do?

741
00:42:29,900 --> 00:42:32,370
Do you want to call and give her a piece of your mind?

742
00:42:33,940 --> 00:42:35,670
Yes, I'll do it.

743
00:42:36,100 --> 00:42:38,640
I'll call and give her a piece of my mind,

744
00:42:39,140 --> 00:42:40,270
so call and put her on the phone, okay?

745
00:42:40,340 --> 00:42:41,780
All right. Hold on.

746
00:42:41,840 --> 00:42:42,840
Okay.

747
00:42:43,850 --> 00:42:47,820
Let's see. H, H. Her last name starts with an H.

748
00:42:48,580 --> 00:42:50,750
H is...

749
00:42:50,820 --> 00:42:52,650
- Oh my! - My gosh!

750
00:42:52,920 --> 00:42:53,920
Baby.

751
00:42:54,160 --> 00:42:56,560
Honey, are you okay? I'm so sorry. Are you okay?

752
00:42:56,620 --> 00:42:57,630
Honey.

753
00:42:59,630 --> 00:43:03,970
I'm sorry. I'm just going to use the restroom.

754
00:43:05,270 --> 00:43:08,340
- Excuse me. Darn it. - Honey, I'm sorry.

755
00:43:10,100 --> 00:43:11,110
Honey.

756
00:43:13,010 --> 00:43:14,010
Are you crazy?

757
00:43:15,840 --> 00:43:17,380
I think you're the one who's crazy.

758
00:43:18,450 --> 00:43:22,550
Sung Wook told me his future wife is the daughter of a CEO.

759
00:43:22,920 --> 00:43:23,920
What's going on here?

760
00:43:24,750 --> 00:43:26,450
Stay out of other people's business.

761
00:43:26,650 --> 00:43:28,020
Did you perhaps lie to him?

762
00:43:29,290 --> 00:43:30,960
What are you going to do?

763
00:43:31,190 --> 00:43:33,530
Don't you dare say anything unnecessary to Sung Wook.

764
00:43:33,590 --> 00:43:35,830
Why would I say anything unnecessary?

765
00:43:37,100 --> 00:43:38,500
I'm telling you things for your own good.

766
00:43:38,570 --> 00:43:39,770
Some sound advice.

767
00:43:39,870 --> 00:43:40,870
Hey.

768
00:43:44,910 --> 00:43:47,210
I'm already on the verge of losing my mind as it is.

769
00:43:48,040 --> 00:43:49,640
Don't you dare say one word about my family...

770
00:43:50,040 --> 00:43:51,610
or what's happening.

771
00:43:51,850 --> 00:43:52,850
We'll see.

772
00:43:53,710 --> 00:43:56,450
When I tell you not to do something, what do you mean, "we'll see?"

773
00:43:57,550 --> 00:44:00,790
What's the point of being so smart...

774
00:44:01,420 --> 00:44:04,860
if you can't even grasp the situation?

775
00:44:05,260 --> 00:44:06,330
What did you say?

776
00:44:06,390 --> 00:44:08,030
I'm the one holding all the cards.

777
00:44:08,660 --> 00:44:12,000
I'm in the position of power, and you're not.

778
00:44:12,770 --> 00:44:14,070
Depending on how you act,

779
00:44:14,670 --> 00:44:16,740
I'll decide whether to grant your request...

780
00:44:16,800 --> 00:44:18,410
or if I should just blow this whole thing wide open.

781
00:44:18,470 --> 00:44:19,540
I'll be the one making that call.

782
00:44:21,240 --> 00:44:23,280
So you'd better watch how you act.

783
00:44:24,380 --> 00:44:25,380
Got it?

784
00:44:31,550 --> 00:44:33,990
Wow, this is amazing.

785
00:44:34,690 --> 00:44:35,990
Oh my.

786
00:44:37,660 --> 00:44:39,790
I heard she loves Joseon Japchae.

787
00:44:40,190 --> 00:44:42,700
I'll make some, so please pick it up tomorrow.

788
00:44:43,200 --> 00:44:45,100
Oh, my goodness. But it's so much work.

789
00:44:45,200 --> 00:44:46,470
You don't have to do that.

790
00:44:46,930 --> 00:44:49,300
Well, then please let me pay for the Joseon Japchae in advance.

791
00:44:49,640 --> 00:44:52,110
No, it's okay. It's a birthday gift for her.

792
00:44:52,710 --> 00:44:53,840
I hope she enjoys it.

793
00:44:55,540 --> 00:44:57,180
You're always so kind. How can I thank you?

794
00:44:57,410 --> 00:44:58,410
Have a good day.

795
00:45:01,020 --> 00:45:02,020
Hope you have a busy day.

796
00:45:02,150 --> 00:45:04,250
- Yes, thank you. - See you tomorrow.

797
00:45:04,320 --> 00:45:05,320
Okay.

798
00:45:07,090 --> 00:45:10,090
(Suragan Side Dishes)

799
00:45:25,410 --> 00:45:27,580
Aren't you leaving? Don't you have a business to run?

800
00:45:28,680 --> 00:45:31,480
I will once you sell me something. Then I can go run my business.

801
00:45:31,910 --> 00:45:33,650
Why are you being so stubborn?

802
00:45:36,750 --> 00:45:38,690
I could say the same about you.

803
00:45:40,320 --> 00:45:43,290
Fine, I'll sell it to you. But this is the only time.

804
00:45:46,790 --> 00:45:48,160
What are you talking about?

805
00:45:48,300 --> 00:45:51,070
If customers want to buy, they buy. If they don't, then they won't.

806
00:45:52,300 --> 00:45:53,570
You're being ridiculous.

807
00:45:53,730 --> 00:45:57,300
Ridiculous? Should we go out and ask people...

808
00:45:57,370 --> 00:45:58,710
who's the one being ridiculous right now?

809
00:46:06,110 --> 00:46:08,450
- What are you doing here? - Oh, you're here.

810
00:46:08,820 --> 00:46:10,850
I'm in a standoff with a tyrannical business owner.

811
00:46:14,260 --> 00:46:18,190
(Suragan Side Dishes)

812
00:46:20,130 --> 00:46:23,400
Hey, she won't sell to me. She's singling me out.

813
00:46:23,860 --> 00:46:24,930
And for no good reason.

814
00:46:25,000 --> 00:46:26,730
She's incredibly nice to everyone else.

815
00:46:26,800 --> 00:46:27,870
She gives them extra side dishes...

816
00:46:28,170 --> 00:46:29,300
and even remembers their birthdays.

817
00:46:29,800 --> 00:46:32,140
- She's only mean to me. - You crazy bastard.

818
00:46:32,840 --> 00:46:34,510
If she won't sell to you, go to another store...

819
00:46:34,580 --> 00:46:36,080
or just come back to the restaurant.

820
00:46:37,110 --> 00:46:39,150
Why are you making a scene in her place of business?

821
00:46:40,050 --> 00:46:41,520
Let go.

822
00:46:41,580 --> 00:46:43,020
I'm not leaving until she sells to me.

823
00:46:43,120 --> 00:46:44,250
Why is she picking on me?

824
00:46:44,420 --> 00:46:46,420
We have to get back and open the restaurant.

825
00:46:47,020 --> 00:46:48,020
Are you really not getting up?

826
00:46:48,360 --> 00:46:50,420
Will you tell customers to suck thumbs instead of pickles?

827
00:46:50,520 --> 00:46:52,230
You can just buy them from another shop.

828
00:46:52,330 --> 00:46:54,860
How can I go to another shop? Nothing else is as good as this.

829
00:46:58,400 --> 00:46:59,400
Here you go.

830
00:47:00,670 --> 00:47:03,140
Here. Take them and please just go.

831
00:47:05,510 --> 00:47:06,610
I'll be back when we run out.

832
00:47:07,310 --> 00:47:08,540
I don't care if you're the owner or what,

833
00:47:08,610 --> 00:47:09,610
but you need to keep him away.

834
00:47:11,980 --> 00:47:13,950
What, is he a goalie and I'm a soccer ball?

835
00:47:14,050 --> 00:47:15,120
Stop what?

836
00:47:16,280 --> 00:47:17,650
Just shut up, Kim Mu Jin.

837
00:47:19,550 --> 00:47:20,550
If you come here again, I'll report you...

838
00:47:20,620 --> 00:47:21,820
to the police for interfering with my business.

839
00:47:21,960 --> 00:47:23,160
Go ahead.

840
00:47:23,560 --> 00:47:25,290
Fine. Then I'll report you to the Consumer Agency.

841
00:47:33,230 --> 00:47:34,400
Are you a grade schooler?

842
00:47:35,340 --> 00:47:37,640
"Fine. Then I'll report you to the Consumer Agency."

843
00:47:38,540 --> 00:47:40,940
- You're so childish. - When was I?

844
00:47:41,410 --> 00:47:43,710
She's just singling me out. She won't sell anything to me.

845
00:47:43,840 --> 00:47:47,350
And you don't discriminate? We ban couples from our restaurant,

846
00:47:47,410 --> 00:47:50,420
- and we ban married people too. - That's completely different.

847
00:47:50,480 --> 00:47:51,490
How is that the same thing?

848
00:47:51,550 --> 00:47:53,620
So it's one rule for you and another for everyone else?

849
00:47:54,020 --> 00:47:55,020
And another thing, man.

850
00:47:55,360 --> 00:47:57,690
Why are you badmouthing the owner?

851
00:47:57,760 --> 00:47:59,460
She gives you tons of stuff on the house, you know?

852
00:47:59,860 --> 00:48:02,200
She's so generous. Even things that aren't on the menu.

853
00:48:02,400 --> 00:48:04,930
Badmouthing? Generous? Taking her side?

854
00:48:06,730 --> 00:48:08,100
What do you mean, taking her side?

855
00:48:10,640 --> 00:48:12,140
Hey, you drive.

856
00:48:12,810 --> 00:48:15,210
- You drive. - Then why did you even buy a car?

857
00:48:33,460 --> 00:48:34,460
Mom.

858
00:48:35,700 --> 00:48:36,700
Gyeol.

859
00:48:37,400 --> 00:48:39,730
Are you okay? I came because I was worried about you.

860
00:48:41,800 --> 00:48:42,800
Why would you be worried about me?

861
00:48:43,270 --> 00:48:44,840
Because of what I said this morning.

862
00:48:44,910 --> 00:48:46,070
I was worried you were dwelling on it.

863
00:48:46,410 --> 00:48:48,810
Actually, I don't need a dad.

864
00:48:51,050 --> 00:48:53,050
- Really? - Really.

865
00:48:53,810 --> 00:48:55,080
I don't believe you.

866
00:48:56,450 --> 00:48:57,450
Is it that obvious?

867
00:49:02,960 --> 00:49:05,160
About the dad situation, just give me some time.

868
00:49:09,860 --> 00:49:13,300
There are lots of good men in the world besides Game Man.

869
00:49:13,830 --> 00:49:15,200
Is Game Man no good?

870
00:49:17,540 --> 00:49:19,310
That's right. He's not.

871
00:49:20,470 --> 00:49:21,480
Mom.

872
00:49:22,410 --> 00:49:24,580
Can we please not talk about Game Man anymore?

873
00:49:28,980 --> 00:49:30,280
Do you smell something burning?

874
00:49:31,590 --> 00:49:34,390
Why? Is it my Gyeol's love for me...

875
00:49:34,490 --> 00:49:35,490
that's burning?

876
00:49:39,230 --> 00:49:40,590
Oh no, I left the seaweed soup on.

877
00:49:40,660 --> 00:49:42,230
Oh, what do I do?

878
00:49:49,140 --> 00:49:51,210
Mom, there's a wallet here.

879
00:49:53,410 --> 00:49:55,680
(ID Card: Kim Mu Jin)

880
00:49:57,610 --> 00:49:58,950
What is wrong with me?

881
00:49:59,010 --> 00:50:01,250
If it weren't for you, Gyeol, I would have been in big trouble.

882
00:50:01,320 --> 00:50:03,580
Mom, was Game Man at the store?

883
00:50:05,490 --> 00:50:08,260
- No. - I think this belongs to Game Man.

884
00:50:12,360 --> 00:50:14,530
Oh, he came by a little while ago to buy some side dishes.

885
00:50:16,700 --> 00:50:18,070
Give it here. I'll put it in a mailbox.

886
00:50:18,230 --> 00:50:19,570
I know where his restaurant is.

887
00:50:19,630 --> 00:50:21,340
I'll just run over and give it to him.

888
00:50:21,470 --> 00:50:22,470
Gyeol.

889
00:50:23,700 --> 00:50:24,710
Gyeol!

890
00:50:24,810 --> 00:50:25,840
(Suragan Side Dishes)

891
00:50:25,910 --> 00:50:28,240
- The stew is ready, right? - Yes.

892
00:50:28,310 --> 00:50:30,240
(Suragan Side Dishes)

893
00:50:44,460 --> 00:50:46,290
I took the White Kimchi and Radish Water Kimchi to the kitchen.

894
00:50:48,460 --> 00:50:49,560
Are you not coming in?

895
00:50:52,000 --> 00:50:53,430
I don't think I can cook today.

896
00:51:02,410 --> 00:51:04,480
Let's give our employees a big raise.

897
00:51:04,950 --> 00:51:07,050
They're covering for you since you're a mess.

898
00:51:07,480 --> 00:51:09,820
Do you realise they're each doing the work of 100 people?

899
00:51:11,120 --> 00:51:12,120
I know.

900
00:51:14,220 --> 00:51:16,120
I was already planning to give them my entire salary.

901
00:51:18,230 --> 00:51:22,800
Why do women like you? You have...

902
00:51:22,860 --> 00:51:24,570
no professionalism whatsoever.

903
00:51:26,870 --> 00:51:28,100
Maybe I should just emigrate.

904
00:51:28,240 --> 00:51:30,140
Did you and Seo Hyun plan this?

905
00:51:31,870 --> 00:51:34,880
Unbelievable. Seo Hyun said she's emigrating too.

906
00:51:37,210 --> 00:51:38,310
Because of you.

907
00:51:38,710 --> 00:51:41,020
She said she can't stand to watch you be a mess anymore,

908
00:51:41,080 --> 00:51:42,780
so she's moving to the country farthest away from here.

909
00:51:45,420 --> 00:51:47,350
Tell Seo Hyun to just stay here.

910
00:51:47,990 --> 00:51:49,960
Where does she think she's going, leaving her family behind?

911
00:51:52,430 --> 00:51:54,500
If anyone should emigrate, it's me.

912
00:51:57,160 --> 00:51:58,170
My gosh.

913
00:51:58,630 --> 00:52:00,030
Judging by your face, you're for real.

914
00:52:00,370 --> 00:52:01,440
Are you really going to go?

915
00:52:06,640 --> 00:52:08,280
I've thought about it a lot,

916
00:52:11,210 --> 00:52:13,810
and I think it's best if I get out of Gyu Rim's way.

917
00:52:17,620 --> 00:52:18,620
She already has a family.

918
00:52:18,690 --> 00:52:20,350
What am I even doing, throwing a tantrum like this?

919
00:52:22,260 --> 00:52:23,290
Am I not crazy?

920
00:52:24,690 --> 00:52:27,830
Well, I can't say you're wrong.

921
00:52:30,730 --> 00:52:32,830
Then what about Han Gyeol?

922
00:52:34,570 --> 00:52:36,000
Is it over with the kid too?

923
00:52:40,370 --> 00:52:42,680
Yes. It's over.

924
00:52:44,240 --> 00:52:45,250
Never again...

925
00:52:47,550 --> 00:52:48,580
You're not going to see him?

926
00:52:51,690 --> 00:52:53,290
I'm not going to see him.

927
00:52:54,690 --> 00:52:55,690
Mister.

928
00:53:00,330 --> 00:53:01,330
Gyeol.

929
00:53:01,400 --> 00:53:02,600
I was at my mom's store,

930
00:53:02,660 --> 00:53:04,330
and I found your wallet on the ground.

931
00:53:05,430 --> 00:53:06,700
I came to return it to you.

932
00:53:08,940 --> 00:53:09,940
Thanks.

933
00:53:13,970 --> 00:53:16,710
Wow, how did you get all the way here?

934
00:53:17,310 --> 00:53:18,310
I took the bus.

935
00:53:19,350 --> 00:53:21,620
But why were you at my mom's store?

936
00:53:22,350 --> 00:53:23,420
To buy some side dishes.

937
00:53:25,890 --> 00:53:26,890
Mister,

938
00:53:27,990 --> 00:53:29,790
are you mad at me?

939
00:53:31,530 --> 00:53:32,530
No.

940
00:53:33,330 --> 00:53:34,330
But...

941
00:53:35,000 --> 00:53:36,460
why are you being so cold?

942
00:53:37,100 --> 00:53:38,100
Am I?

943
00:53:38,730 --> 00:53:39,730
No, I'm not.

944
00:53:39,800 --> 00:53:41,970
Mister, you're acting really weird today.

945
00:53:42,570 --> 00:53:44,000
Why aren't you smiling?

946
00:53:48,610 --> 00:53:50,110
Don't force yourself to smile.

947
00:53:57,650 --> 00:53:59,390
Just act normal.

948
00:53:59,450 --> 00:54:01,460
You're going to make the kid cry, you idiot.

949
00:54:10,760 --> 00:54:11,770
Gyeol, have you had dinner?

950
00:54:13,270 --> 00:54:14,570
Do you want to have dinner with me?

951
00:54:16,040 --> 00:54:17,400
Now you seem like yourself again.

952
00:54:20,740 --> 00:54:22,940
You said you came by bus, right? I'll give you a ride home.

953
00:54:23,310 --> 00:54:24,310
Thank you.

954
00:54:24,880 --> 00:54:25,880
I'll be back.

955
00:54:26,210 --> 00:54:28,220
- Goodbye. - Bye now.

956
00:54:28,880 --> 00:54:29,980
There we go.

957
00:54:30,550 --> 00:54:32,790
- You found my wallet. - Yes.

958
00:54:48,440 --> 00:54:49,540
Bye, Gyeol.

959
00:54:50,070 --> 00:54:51,170
Come again.

960
00:54:54,910 --> 00:54:56,810
Well, what can you do about blood ties?

961
00:54:57,810 --> 00:54:59,180
Is he really his son, though?

962
00:55:03,980 --> 00:55:05,450
You scared me.

963
00:55:06,150 --> 00:55:08,090
Who's that little kid leaving with Mu Jin?

964
00:55:10,460 --> 00:55:12,560
Why does he have such a sweet look on his face?

965
00:55:13,530 --> 00:55:15,130
You know, if someone didn't know better,

966
00:55:15,200 --> 00:55:17,360
they'd think they were father and son.

967
00:55:17,560 --> 00:55:18,570
I know, right?

968
00:55:19,370 --> 00:55:21,440
You feel that family bond too, don't you?

969
00:55:24,000 --> 00:55:25,110
What are you talking about?

970
00:55:26,270 --> 00:55:29,010
(Son)

971
00:55:37,020 --> 00:55:38,850
Why aren't you answering your phone, Han Gyeol?

972
00:55:40,920 --> 00:55:41,920
Hello.

973
00:55:43,920 --> 00:55:45,490
Why are you answering Gyeol's phone, Father?

974
00:55:46,190 --> 00:55:47,590
Well, it was ringing, so I answered.

975
00:55:47,860 --> 00:55:49,860
Gyeol left his phone at home and went out.

976
00:55:53,630 --> 00:55:54,640
Here you go.

977
00:55:59,410 --> 00:56:01,140
Thank you for the ride.

978
00:56:01,340 --> 00:56:03,940
- Okay, get home safe. - Okay.

979
00:56:04,210 --> 00:56:07,050
- Han Gyeol. - Uncle Gyu Seo. Aunt Gyu Min.

980
00:56:07,580 --> 00:56:09,950
(Han Gyu Seo, Han Gyu Min)

981
00:56:15,790 --> 00:56:17,320
Gyu Seo and Gyu Min?

982
00:56:18,590 --> 00:56:21,230
Yes. You're Mu Jin, aren't you?

983
00:56:22,560 --> 00:56:23,800
Yes, that's right.

984
00:56:25,230 --> 00:56:26,270
You must be Gyu Seo.

985
00:56:26,900 --> 00:56:29,070
- Have you been well? - Yes.

986
00:56:29,900 --> 00:56:30,900
And you're Gyu Min?

987
00:56:32,170 --> 00:56:33,170
Yes.

988
00:56:35,080 --> 00:56:36,180
It's good to see you.

989
00:56:36,710 --> 00:56:38,250
It's really been a long time.

990
00:56:38,780 --> 00:56:40,650
I wouldn't have recognised you if I'd passed you on the street.

991
00:56:45,190 --> 00:56:46,190
- If you're not busy, - If you're not busy,

992
00:56:46,290 --> 00:56:47,450
- could we talk for a moment? - could we talk for a moment?

993
00:56:47,550 --> 00:56:49,260
(Han Gyu Min)

994
00:56:51,830 --> 00:56:52,830
Me first.

995
00:56:53,290 --> 00:56:54,290
Me first.

996
00:56:54,460 --> 00:56:55,560
Just say it together.

997
00:56:57,030 --> 00:56:58,030
Okay.

998
00:56:58,100 --> 00:56:59,900
(Han Gyu Min)

999
00:57:00,630 --> 00:57:02,640
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

1000
00:57:03,540 --> 00:57:04,540
Here.

1001
00:57:07,640 --> 00:57:09,010
- This is delicious. - Yes.

1002
00:57:09,740 --> 00:57:10,740
It's delicious.

1003
00:57:11,680 --> 00:57:12,680
Have another.

1004
00:57:15,020 --> 00:57:16,020
Thank you.

1005
00:57:17,950 --> 00:57:18,950
Well...

1006
00:57:19,590 --> 00:57:21,120
So what is it? Go on, tell me.

1007
00:57:24,490 --> 00:57:25,490
You go first.

1008
00:57:25,960 --> 00:57:26,960
No, you go first.

1009
00:57:29,030 --> 00:57:30,230
Do you two want to say it together?

1010
00:57:31,570 --> 00:57:32,600
No, not that.

1011
00:57:33,600 --> 00:57:34,600
Mister.

1012
00:57:35,500 --> 00:57:36,870
I heard you're not married yet.

1013
00:57:37,700 --> 00:57:38,710
That's right.

1014
00:57:39,070 --> 00:57:40,140
Are you seeing anyone?

1015
00:57:43,180 --> 00:57:44,180
No.

1016
00:57:46,310 --> 00:57:48,350
You're still not over my oldest sister, are you?

1017
00:57:49,520 --> 00:57:50,520
Han Gyu Seo.

1018
00:57:53,690 --> 00:57:56,360
My sister is completely over you, just so you know.

1019
00:57:57,360 --> 00:57:58,360
No, she hasn't.

1020
00:57:58,790 --> 00:58:00,730
She still really likes him. I know it.

1021
00:58:00,990 --> 00:58:03,360
- What do you know? - Gyeol said so.

1022
00:58:03,700 --> 00:58:06,170
He said he thinks she still really likes Mu Jin.

1023
00:58:06,900 --> 00:58:10,140
That all ended eight years ago. She had such a hard time back then.

1024
00:58:10,200 --> 00:58:11,270
How much she...

1025
00:58:12,610 --> 00:58:13,710
cried all on her own.

1026
00:58:13,770 --> 00:58:15,810
That's because she liked him so much...

1027
00:58:15,880 --> 00:58:17,240
I'm telling you, it's all in the past.

1028
00:58:18,080 --> 00:58:19,810
Her wounds were finally starting to heal,

1029
00:58:19,980 --> 00:58:21,210
so why are you trying to reopen them?

1030
00:58:21,280 --> 00:58:23,180
I don't want to see my sister suffering anymore.

1031
00:58:23,880 --> 00:58:25,620
Hey, you two, stop fighting.

1032
00:58:26,920 --> 00:58:28,620
So, what is it exactly that you wanted to say?

1033
00:58:31,730 --> 00:58:34,560
I want you and my oldest sister to get back together.

1034
00:58:35,630 --> 00:58:36,630
I'm against it.

1035
00:58:37,100 --> 00:58:40,100
I want you to stay away from my sister.

1036
00:58:43,500 --> 00:58:44,770
Okay, well...

1037
00:58:45,410 --> 00:58:47,210
I understand where you both stand.

1038
00:58:48,380 --> 00:58:49,380
I really do.

1039
00:58:51,280 --> 00:58:52,580
I'll do what Gyu Min says.

1040
00:58:54,080 --> 00:58:56,020
After today, I won't go anywhere near your sister.

1041
00:58:56,080 --> 00:58:57,950
You'll never see me hanging around her again.

1042
00:58:58,250 --> 00:59:00,420
- Mister. - Thank you.

1043
00:59:01,220 --> 00:59:02,490
Please, try to be brave again.

1044
00:59:03,220 --> 00:59:04,960
My sister still hasn't gotten over you.

1045
00:59:05,060 --> 00:59:06,060
I'm telling you.

1046
00:59:07,630 --> 00:59:09,660
I admit I may have lost my mind for a moment,

1047
00:59:10,200 --> 00:59:11,630
but I don't have affairs.

1048
00:59:12,030 --> 00:59:13,130
An affair?

1049
00:59:14,130 --> 00:59:15,140
Who?

1050
00:59:15,200 --> 00:59:16,700
Your sister is married, isn't she?

1051
00:59:16,770 --> 00:59:19,770
That's not true. What do you mean she's married?

1052
00:59:20,770 --> 00:59:23,940
My sister isn't married. She's raising Gyeol on her own.

1053
00:59:27,850 --> 00:59:29,450
She's not married?

1054
00:59:31,150 --> 00:59:32,150
Hey.

1055
00:59:32,620 --> 00:59:34,120
You're the one who lied that she was married, aren't you?

1056
00:59:34,190 --> 00:59:36,020
Just to keep her and Mu Jin apart.

1057
00:59:36,160 --> 00:59:38,890
Hey, this is the first time I've ever met him.

1058
00:59:54,510 --> 00:59:56,380
(Taking care of my grandchild is my greatest joy these days.)

1059
01:00:01,210 --> 01:00:02,220
Honestly...

1060
01:00:12,630 --> 01:00:14,900
(Our angel's off to dreamland. Isn’t he just so cute and lovable?)

1061
01:00:16,500 --> 01:00:17,500
Unbelievable.

1062
01:00:29,610 --> 01:00:30,810
Chairman Kim.

1063
01:00:31,510 --> 01:00:32,710
Listen.

1064
01:00:33,610 --> 01:00:35,880
Your grandson going to the play cafe,

1065
01:00:35,950 --> 01:00:37,680
eating, playing, sleeping, and pooping...

1066
01:00:37,750 --> 01:00:39,350
Why are you sending all of this to me?

1067
01:00:40,020 --> 01:00:43,320
How many of these do you send me in a single day?

1068
01:00:43,860 --> 01:00:46,290
This is harassment. You get that?

1069
01:00:47,160 --> 01:00:49,900
And let's be honest here.

1070
01:00:50,700 --> 01:00:53,900
Frankly, your grandson is only cute to you.

1071
01:00:54,130 --> 01:00:55,940
He looks like a squashed steamed bun...

1072
01:00:57,270 --> 01:00:58,270
Oh, whatever.

1073
01:00:59,370 --> 01:01:02,140
Don't send me stuff like this ever again, okay?

1074
01:01:02,410 --> 01:01:04,740
If you send me one more, I'm blocking you.

1075
01:01:06,350 --> 01:01:08,950
What? You think I'm being nasty?

1076
01:01:10,120 --> 01:01:12,620
What? "Jealousy is defeat..." Hey.

1077
01:01:13,220 --> 01:01:15,960
Don't call me for a while. I'm hanging up.

1078
01:01:18,760 --> 01:01:20,090
That rotten woman.

1079
01:01:20,630 --> 01:01:23,100
Honestly, her grandson is only cute to her.

1080
01:01:23,360 --> 01:01:26,530
Why is she showing him off and making such a big fuss?

1081
01:01:27,200 --> 01:01:30,370
Is she the only person in the world with a grandchild? Honestly.

1082
01:01:30,840 --> 01:01:32,270
But you don't have any grandchildren, Mom.

1083
01:01:33,710 --> 01:01:35,180
You've gotten really mouthy lately, haven't you?

1084
01:01:36,110 --> 01:01:37,440
If you had a grandchild, Mom,

1085
01:01:37,510 --> 01:01:39,650
I bet you'd be way worse than Min Ja.

1086
01:01:39,880 --> 01:01:42,120
Then go have a baby and bring one to me.

1087
01:01:42,180 --> 01:01:44,350
Have one and then we'll see how I act.

1088
01:01:45,220 --> 01:01:46,390
No thanks, I'm good.

1089
01:01:47,520 --> 01:01:49,560
But it might be possible with Mu Jin, right?

1090
01:01:50,720 --> 01:01:52,930
I told you not to bring him up.

1091
01:01:56,860 --> 01:01:58,570
What if Mu Jin...

1092
01:01:58,770 --> 01:02:02,800
- had a son? What would you do then? - I told you not to talk about...

1093
01:02:05,610 --> 01:02:06,940
What did you just say?

1094
01:02:08,680 --> 01:02:10,610
It's not confirmed yet, but...

1095
01:02:12,550 --> 01:02:13,950
Today...

1096
01:02:14,580 --> 01:02:17,250
I think I saw Mu Jin's son, Mom.

1097
01:02:22,190 --> 01:02:23,190
What?

1098
01:02:24,460 --> 01:02:27,460
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

1099
01:02:47,350 --> 01:02:48,580
Han Gyu Rim.

1100
01:03:00,760 --> 01:03:02,230
I came because there's something I need to say.

1101
01:03:12,140 --> 01:03:13,470
For everything...

1102
01:03:16,010 --> 01:03:17,410
I'm so sorry.

1103
01:03:24,420 --> 01:03:26,190
I won't bother you again.

1104
01:03:33,630 --> 01:03:34,990
As long as we're alive...

1105
01:03:38,930 --> 01:03:40,870
Let's never see each other again.

1106
01:04:45,630 --> 01:04:47,170
(Love on the Menu)

1107
01:04:47,600 --> 01:04:51,500
You said you were married? I told him you're not married.

1108
01:04:51,600 --> 01:04:54,140
So, stop putting up a wall and running away.

1109
01:04:54,310 --> 01:04:56,810
Just make a move already.

1110
01:04:57,080 --> 01:04:58,750
He got hurt because of me.

1111
01:04:59,150 --> 01:05:02,080
Who? I said I'll take care of him.

1112
01:05:02,150 --> 01:05:04,380
Don't be so quick to say you'll take responsibility.

1113
01:05:04,450 --> 01:05:05,890
They're saying Gyeol's father is back. So what now?

1114
01:05:05,890 --> 01:05:09,260
If he really is Mu Jin's son, what are you going to do?

1115
01:05:09,320 --> 01:05:11,220
We'll have to bring him here and raise him properly.

1116
01:05:11,590 --> 01:05:12,830
You're joking, right?

1117
01:05:13,060 --> 01:05:14,860
- I'm not joking. - What's with you and Jo Heung Sik?

1118
01:05:15,360 --> 01:05:16,460
Are you two dating?

